cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "Delhi Public Services Index (PSI) pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for the Delhi Public Services Index: settlement
  polygons, point and line services, barriers, adjacency, decay, overlap
  lending, category exclusion and the composite index, driven by YAML
  methodology profiles with an independent reference implementation and
  fixture-based pins.
authors:
  - family-names: Bell
    given-names: Bob
    email: bwbelljr@gmail.com
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
repository-code: "https://github.com/bwbelljr/delhi_spatial_index"
keywords:
  - urban inequality
  - public services
  - spatial index
  - Delhi
  - reproducibility
# `license:` is deliberately absent until DEL-56 chooses one — CFF allows the
# field to be omitted, and a wrong value is worse than none. Add the chosen
# SPDX identifier here and in pyproject.toml at the same time.
